// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6001 new: 13 Linux detection rules
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6001
// Pull request author: saakovv
// Change: new rule
// Title: Linux Reverse Shell or Code Execution via Rview Binary
// Sigma ID: b2d7c3f1-4e8a-4b43-c1d2-3f9e5a8b7c20
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Ivan Saakov
// Date: 2026-05-10 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059.006
// Description: Detects suspicious use of the rview binary with embedded scripting arguments that can spawn
//   shells, establish network connections, or load shared libraries. Rview is the restricted view
//   mode of Vim, but it supports Python and Lua scripting via :py and :lua commands, enabling full
//   shell execution despite its restricted designation. When combined with os.execl, os.execute, or
//   socket.connect patterns, rview can be used to establish reverse shells or execute arbitrary
//   commands, particularly when run with SUID or sudo.
// False positives:
//   - Security researchers testing GTFOBins techniques in an isolated environment
//   - Unlikely in production environments
// References:
//   - https://gtfobins.github.io/gtfobins/rview/
//   - https://vimdoc.sourceforge.net/htmldoc/if_pyth.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/e5bac28da3655c33390db7ef1503db8cd3babb5f/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_rview_shell_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "/rview" or FolderPath endswith "/rvim") and (ProcessCommandLine contains ":py" or ProcessCommandLine contains ":lua" or ProcessCommandLine contains "os.execl" or ProcessCommandLine contains "os.execute" or ProcessCommandLine contains "exec sh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "pty.spawn" or ProcessCommandLine contains "socket.connect" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/sh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/bin/bash" or ProcessCommandLine contains "cap_setuid" or ProcessCommandLine contains "sudo rview")
